<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robben Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robben Island is a small island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-bay">Table Bay</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. From the 17th century it was used to banish and imprison opponents of colonial rule, and under apartheid it held political prisoners, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>, who spent eighteen of his twenty-seven years in prison there. It is now a museum and was declared a World Heritage Site in 1999.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robben-island.jpg" alt="Robben Island" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: South African Tourism from South Africa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robben_Island_-_Cape_Town,_South_Africa_(3883849594).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
